{"event": "bridge_rerank_request", "stage": ["dagbt", "set_reranker", "64", "batch", "0"], "node_id": "detective", "scoring_query": "What is the name of the fictional private detective that appears in \"The Adventure of the Seven Clocks\"?", "scoring_context_id": "f751db736af6df29a9c2a41798f3222ccfdcff972b6cee8bb575a0bb488e2867", "algorithm_version": "dagbt_local_terminal_v1", "query": "What is the name of the fictional private detective that appears in \"The Adventure of the Seven Clocks\"?", "documents": ["Factual evidence passages:\n[Passage {\"doc_id\": \"hotpotqa:13\", \"source_id\": \"hotpotqa:13\"}]\nThe Adventure of the Seven Clocks\n\"The Adventure of the Seven Clocks\" is a Sherlock Holmes story by Adrian Conan Doyle and John Dickson Carr. The story was published in the 1954 collection, \"The Exploits of Sherlock Holmes\".\n\n[Passage {\"doc_id\": \"hotpotqa:15\", \"source_id\": \"hotpotqa:15\"}]\nNick Carter, Master Detective\nNick Carter, Master Detective was a Mutual radio crime drama based on tales of the fictional private detective Nick Carter from Street & Smith's dime novels and pulp magazines. Nick Carter first came to radio as The Return of Nick Carter, a reference to the character's pulp origins, but the title was soon changed to Nick Carter, Master Detective. A veteran radio dramatist, Ferrin Fraser, wrote many of the scripts.\n\n[Passage {\"doc_id\": \"hotpotqa:2607\", \"source_id\": \"hotpotqa:2607\"}]\nHe Who Whispers\nHe Who Whispers is a mystery novel (1946) by detective novelist John Dickson Carr. Like Many of the works by this author feature so-called impossible crimes (for the most part, falling into the category of the locked room mystery). In this case, the novel falls into a smaller category of Carr's work in that it is suggested that the crime is the work of a supernatural being (here, a vampire). The detective is Dr. Gideon Fell, who ultimately uncovers a rational explanation for the novel's events. Carr considered this one of his best impossible crime novels."], "document_offset": 0, "logical_document_count": 1, "physical_batch_limit": 4, "score_contract": "pointwise", "score_space": "unit_interval", "sequence": 1576, "elapsed_seconds": 113.11817073822021}
